# Trivy suppressions — one vulnerability ID per line, each with a reason.
# Revisit these whenever the underlying package or its usage changes.
#
# The two entries below are reported for pip's VENDORED copies
# (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt), not for our application dependencies:
#   - GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  → pip vendors msgpack 1.1.2 (CacheControl dep)
#   - CVE-2025-47273       → pip vendors setuptools 70.3.0 (build isolation)
# The production container never executes pip, and the vendored code is not
# reachable from the app. Real application dependencies are still audited by
# pip-audit in the `test` job, and Dependabot keeps pip itself fresh via the
# base image.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
